<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sebetwane</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1790s–<a href="/years/1851">1851</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Sebitwane</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sebitwane was the founder of the Kololo kingdom, a Sotho-speaking leader who led his people north from the highveld during the upheavals of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mfecane">Mfecane</a> in the 1820s and 1830s. Around 1840 he conquered the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lozi-people">Lozi</a> kingdom of Barotseland on the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zambezi">Zambezi</a>. He met the missionary <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david-livingstone">David Livingstone</a> in 1851, shortly before his death.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sebetwane.jpg" alt="Sebetwane" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: VerraaierABO · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Biddulphsberg._03.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
